-- title:
--   Étale coordinate and residue character at a smooth special point
-- statement:
--   Let $A$ be a discrete valuation ring which is a domain, $\varpi \in A$ an element with $\mathfrak m_A = (\varpi)$, and assume the residue field $\kappa = A/\mathfrak m_A$ is algebraically closed. Let $L$ be a fraction field of $A$ and $F$ a field that is an $L$-algebra and an $A$-algebra compatibly, let $j \in F$ be nonzero and transcendental over $L$, and assume $F$ is finite-dimensional and separable over the intermediate field $L(j)$. Write $\mathfrak X$ for the two-chart integral model [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel A F j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236), the pushout of the two maps from the middle chart to $X_{\mathrm{fin}} = \operatorname{Spec} B_{\mathrm{fin}}$ and $X_\infty = \operatorname{Spec} B_\infty$, where $B_{\mathrm{fin}}$ (resp. $B_\infty$) is the subalgebra of elements of $F$ integral over $A[j]$ (resp. over $A[j^{-1}]$), and write $\mathfrak X \to \operatorname{Spec} A$ for the structural morphism obtained from the two structure maps of the charts. Let $x \in \mathfrak X$ satisfy: $x$ maps to the closed point of $\operatorname{Spec} A$; $x$ specialises only to itself; and $x$ has an open neighbourhood $U$ such that the inclusion of $U$ followed by $\mathfrak X \to \operatorname{Spec} A$ is smooth. The assertion is the existence of a subring $S \subseteq F$, a ring homomorphism $\varphi : A[T] \to S$ and a ring homomorphism $\chi : S \to \kappa$ with all of the following. (i) An element $f \in F$ lies in $S$ precisely when, for every prime $y$ of $B_{\mathrm{fin}}$ whose image in $\mathfrak X$ is $x$, there are $g, h \in B_{\mathrm{fin}}$ with $h \notin y$ and $fh = g$, and likewise for every prime of $B_\infty$ lying over $x$. (ii) For $f \in S$, $\chi(f) = 0$ precisely when such $g, h$ can be chosen in each chart with, in addition, $g \in y$. (iii) $S$ contains the image of $A$ in $F$, $\varphi(a)$ is the image of $a$ in $F$ for constants $a \in A$, $\chi(\varphi(a))$ is the residue of $a$, and $\chi(\varphi(T)) = 0$. (iv) $S$ admits a local ring structure for which $\ker \chi$ is the maximal ideal and that maximal ideal is generated by $\varphi(\varpi)$ and $\varphi(T)$; moreover $\chi$ is surjective. (v) $\varphi$ is formally smooth, formally unramified and essentially of finite type, and $\varphi(T) \notin (\varphi(\varpi))$. (vi) Every $f \in F$ is of the form $g/h$ with $g, h \in S$, $h \neq 0$. (vii) $S$ is Noetherian, and $S/(\varphi(\varpi))$ is a domain and a discrete valuation ring.
--
--   This is a packaging statement: at a closed point of the special fibre lying in the smooth locus, the local ring of the two-chart integral model is presented concretely as a subring $S$ of the function field $F$, described by chart fractions regular at $x$, equipped with an étale coordinate $A[T] \to S$, the evaluation character to the residue field of $A$, a description of the maximal ideal, Noetherianity, and regularity of the fibre $S/(\varpi)$. It is used by the full-level modular curve statements that produce stalks with étale coordinates and residue characters at points off the branch locus, from which the integral models read the two-chart construction.
